1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,975
Whiskers is faster than me!

2
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:07,700
Wow... This is the most beautiful sunset in the world!

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:17,334
Faster than me. The most beautiful sunset in the world. Mia is comparing things. We do this every day, so let's learn comparatives and superlatives.

4
00:00:17,934 --> 00:00:22,313
By the end, you'll know the rules, the irregular forms, and the mistakes to avoid.

5
00:00:23,263 --> 00:00:24,748
First, the idea.

6
00:00:25,348 --> 00:00:30,094
We use the comparative to compare two things: Whiskers is faster than Mia.

7
00:00:30,694 --> 00:00:37,189
We use the superlative for one thing in a group of three or more: Whiskers is the fastest cat in the village.

8
00:00:38,289 --> 00:00:42,870
Look at Whiskers jump! He's quicker than a bird, and braver than any other cat.

9
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:47,666
Short adjectives, with one syllable, add e r and e s t.

10
00:00:48,266 --> 00:00:50,127
Tall, taller than, the tallest.

11
00:00:50,727 --> 00:00:55,309
If it ends in e, just add r or s t: nice, nicer, the nicest.

12
00:00:55,909 --> 00:00:59,625
One vowel and one consonant? Double it: big, bigger, the biggest.

13
00:01:00,225 --> 00:01:03,650
Hot, hotter, the hottest. Muscat is hotter than London.

14
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:07,614
Adjectives ending in y change the y to i.

15
00:01:08,214 --> 00:01:10,198
Happy, happier, the happiest.

16
00:01:10,798 --> 00:01:12,757
Easy, easier, the easiest.

17
00:01:13,357 --> 00:01:15,294
Funny, funnier, the funniest.

18
00:01:16,244 --> 00:01:20,611
Longer adjectives use more and the most. We don't change the adjective.

19
00:01:21,211 --> 00:01:24,002
Beautiful, more beautiful than, the most beautiful.

20
00:01:24,602 --> 00:01:27,846
Expensive, more expensive than, the most expensive.

21
00:01:28,446 --> 00:01:31,657
Interesting, more interesting than, the most interesting.

22
00:01:32,607 --> 00:01:35,819
And three irregular ones. You must learn them by heart.

23
00:01:36,419 --> 00:01:38,003
Good, better, the best.

24
00:01:38,603 --> 00:01:40,303
Bad, worse, the worst.

25
00:01:40,903 --> 00:01:43,339
Far, farther or further, the farthest.

26
00:01:44,239 --> 00:01:48,564
Wow... This is the most beautiful sunset in the world!

27
00:01:49,014 --> 00:01:50,954
A quick pronunciation tip.

28
00:01:51,554 --> 00:01:54,271
Than is weak and short: taller than. Better than.

29
00:01:54,871 --> 00:01:57,411
The is also weak: the best. The biggest.

30
00:01:58,011 --> 00:02:01,852
And the e r ending is a soft sound: bigger, faster, older.

31
00:02:02,452 --> 00:02:06,363
For the t h sound, put your tongue between your teeth. Than. The.

32
00:02:07,313 --> 00:02:10,454
When two things are the same, use as, adjective, as.

33
00:02:11,054 --> 00:02:13,185
Mia is as tall as her friend.

34
00:02:13,785 --> 00:02:18,708
For a difference, say not as, adjective, as: Whiskers is not as big as a dog.

35
00:02:19,308 --> 00:02:21,687
Today is not as hot as yesterday.

36
00:02:22,287 --> 00:02:24,587
So not as big as means smaller than.

37
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:32,411
From the hill, Mia can see the whole valley. This is the highest place in the village, and the river looks smaller than a ribbon.

38
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:35,039
Some useful questions.

39
00:02:35,639 --> 00:02:41,534
Which is bigger, the sun or the moon? The sun is much bigger. Notice much, it makes the difference stronger.

40
00:02:42,134 --> 00:02:46,082
Who is the oldest in your family? My grandma is the oldest.

41
00:02:46,682 --> 00:02:48,830
What's the best film you've ever seen?

42
00:02:49,730 --> 00:02:52,618
Is the river deeper than the lake?

43
00:02:53,068 --> 00:02:54,848
Now the common mistakes.

44
00:02:55,448 --> 00:02:59,145
He is more tall than me. Tall is short, so: he is taller than me.

45
00:02:59,745 --> 00:03:03,555
She is more better. Better is already a comparative: she is better.

46
00:03:04,155 --> 00:03:06,860
It's the most big house. It's the biggest house.

47
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:12,118
Muscat is hotter from Dubai. We use than: Muscat is hotter than Dubai.

48
00:03:12,718 --> 00:03:17,144
He is tallest in class. Don't forget the: he is the tallest in the class.

49
00:03:18,094 --> 00:03:20,744
Your turn. Listen, then say it out loud.

50
00:03:21,644 --> 00:03:23,702
My bag is heavier than yours.

51
00:03:26,702 --> 00:03:28,576
This is the best day ever!

52
00:03:31,376 --> 00:03:33,517
English is easier than I thought.

53
00:03:36,617 --> 00:03:38,542
She's not as tall as her brother.

54
00:03:41,642 --> 00:03:43,540
It's the most beautiful place.

55
00:03:46,590 --> 00:03:50,348
A short story. Listen for e r, e s t, more and most.

56
00:03:51,448 --> 00:03:58,133
Mia and Whiskers race home along the path. Whiskers is faster, but Mia is cleverer. She knows the shortest way.

57
00:03:59,033 --> 00:04:01,808
Whiskers is faster than me!

58
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:08,726
The grass is softer here, and the evening is warmer than yesterday. For Mia, it's the happiest walk of the year.

59
00:04:09,758 --> 00:04:12,765
Quiz time! Five questions, five seconds each.

60
00:04:13,715 --> 00:04:16,572
Number 1. An elephant is blank than a horse.

61
00:04:22,372 --> 00:04:24,185
Bigger, with double g.

62
00:04:25,085 --> 00:04:28,054
Number 2. This is the blank book in the library.

63
00:04:33,854 --> 00:04:36,601
Most interesting. It's a long adjective.

64
00:04:37,501 --> 00:04:40,679
Number 3. My cold is blank today than yesterday.

65
00:04:46,479 --> 00:04:48,326
Worse. Bad, worse, the worst.

66
00:04:49,226 --> 00:04:51,934
Number 4. Mia is as tall blank her friend.

67
00:04:57,734 --> 00:04:59,207
As. As tall as.

68
00:05:00,107 --> 00:05:03,185
Number 5. Sunday is the blank day of the week.

69
00:05:08,985 --> 00:05:11,141
Happiest. Y changes to i.

70
00:05:12,041 --> 00:05:18,180
Let's remember. Comparatives compare two things, with than. Superlatives pick one from a group, with the.

71
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:25,298
Short adjectives add e r and e s t, y becomes i, and long adjectives use more and the most.

72
00:05:25,898 --> 00:05:29,505
And learn the irregulars: good, better, best. Bad, worse, worst.

73
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:37,169
Your homework: compare two people in your family, and write about the best place in your town. Share it in the comments.

74
00:05:37,769 --> 00:05:40,872
Subscribe for more lessons. See you next time. Bye!

